Add method replayStoryLine near advanceStory. Also stop speech on advance? Actually when advancing line, `renderStoryLine` speaks next and cancels previous. When advancing during typing to finalize text, no change. Good. But what about tapping story close while voice playing — closeModal stop.

Add:
```js
replayStoryLine() {
  const v = this.storyView;
  if (!v) return;
  if (v.mode === 'reply') this.audio?.speakLine('narrator', v.text);
  else if (v.mode === 'dialogue') {
    const line = v.mission.lines[v.line];
    if (line) this.audio?.speakLine(line.s, line.t);
  }
}
```
Need mode could be 'choice'; button hidden there (storyText cleared, choices shown, storyVoice remains? In showStoryChoice we set `$('storyNext').style.visibility='hidden'` but voice button would still be visible. We should hide it in showStoryChoice, and in reply show it again. Let's handle.

Also update `showStoryChoice` to hide voice button? It could replay prompt. We could make it replay the prompt. Actually the voice button could stay visible and replay the prompt. That's nice. But `storyView` mode is 'choice' and replayStoryLine currently handles prompt if `choice` mode. Let's implement:
```js
if (v.mode === 'choice') this.audio?.speakLine('narrator', v.mission.choice?.prompt || '');
```
Need the speaker label "DECISION". Fine.

The voice button's `storyVoice` is within story foot which persists in dialogue shell; when showing choice, the shell remains (it's the same dialogue modal). So keep visible and speak prompt. Good.

But when showing reply, the voice button remains and speaks reply.

Let's add method.

input.newString:
advanceStory() {
  const v = this.storyView;
  if (!v) return;
  if (v.mode === 'reply') { this.finishReply(); return; }
  if (v.mode !== 'dialogue') return;
  if (v.typing) {
    v.typing = false;
    clearInterval(this.typeTimer);
    $('storyText').textContent = v.text;
    $('storyText').classList.remove('typing');
    return;
  }
  v.line++;
  if (v.line >= v.mission.lines.length) this.afterDialogue();
  else { this.audio?.click(); this.renderStoryLine(); }
}

replayStoryLine() {
  const v = this.storyView;
  if (!v) return;
  if (v.mode === 'dialogue') {
    const line = v.mission.lines[v.line];
    if (line) this.audio?.speakLine(line.s, line.t);
  } else if (v.mode === 'choice') {
    const prompt = v.mission.choice?.prompt;
    if (prompt) this.audio?.speakLine('narrator', prompt);
  } else if (v.mode === 'reply' && v.text) {
    this.audio?.speakLine('narrator', v.text);
  }
}

